"'''Say You Won't Let Go'''" is a song by English singer and songwriter [[James Arthur]]. The song was released as a [[Music download|digital download]] on 9 September 2016 in the United Kingdom by [[Columbia Records]] as the lead single from his second studio album ''[[Back from the Edge]]'' (2016).<ref name="iTunes">{{cite web|url=https://music.apple.com/gb/album/say-you-wont-let-go-single/1151197696|title=Say You Won't Let Go – Single by James Arthur on Apple Music|website=iTunes|date=9 September 2016}}</ref> The single peaked at the top of the [[UK Singles Chart]], a position it maintained for three weeks. Outside the United Kingdom, the single has topped the charts in Australia, New Zealand, Sweden and the Republic of Ireland. It also became his breakthrough hit in the US, peaking at number 11 on the [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]]. In early March, it had gone double platinum in the UK.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://twitter.com/JamesArthur23/status/837740019997630466|title=James Arthur on Twitter |publisher=[[Twitter]] |date=3 March 2017|access-date=5 March 2017}}</ref> In May 2018, it was reported that [[the Script]] had launched legal proceedings against Arthur due to alleged copyright infringement in regards to the song.<ref name="Independent">{{cite web|url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/music/news/the-script-james-arthur-sue-copyright-infringement-say-you-wont-let-go-a8364681.html|title=The Script sue James Arthur for copyright infringement over 'Say You Won't Let Go'|website=Independent|date=23 May 2018}}</ref>

In response to claims that the song sounds similar to [[the Script]]'s "[[The Man Who Can't Be Moved]]", the song's writers initially decided not to pursue legal action.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.msn.com/en-gb/news/other/james-arthur-wont-face-legal-action-from-the-script/ar-AAmPkuJ|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170424100607/http://www.msn.com/en-gb/news/other/james-arthur-wont-face-legal-action-from-the-script/ar-AAmPkuJ|url-status=dead|archive-date=24 April 2017|title=James Arthur won't face legal action from The Script|date=11 February 2017|publisher=[[MSN]]|access-date=16 August 2017}}</ref> However, following a claim in May 2018, they were successfully awarded a songwriting credit.<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/articles/business/8457167/james-arthurs-say-you-wont-let-go-copyright-script-lawsuit|title=James Arthur's 'Say You Won't Let Go' Sued for Copyright Infringement by The Script|last=Brooks|first=David|date=21 May 2018|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|access-date=22 May 2018}}</ref>

